  "body": "When the user clicks the cancel button of a file input dialog, there are generally no events dispatched. Some browsers (Chrome and Safari) will clear the input's value and fire a change event, but this only happens if the control had a value previously. \r\n\r\nChrome and Safari also have observable side-effects, such as the window losing and re-gaining focus. \r\n\r\nIdeally a cancel event should be fired so the web page can respond appropriately.",
